IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc20-part16-review.l4 -- sections 520 to 523 of the Criminal Code (Canada): review of a release or detention order by a judge (on the accused's application, s 520, and on the prosecutor's, s 521), interim release
-- by a judge only for the offences of s 469 (s 522), and how long an appearance notice, summons, undertaking or release order lasts and may be vacated or varied (s 523). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text; nothing is claimed verified against the official text.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); a "may" whose gate is "where", "when" or
-- "upon" answers JUST FALSE under the guide's ruling (b) and is counted in the fork register; a duty and a bar answer JUST FALSE when their gate fails.
-- Periods: "two clear days", "three clear days" and "30 days" are counted by the caller as a NUMBER ("clear days" has no counting rule in this Part); 30 days from the decision are counted with `Date to days`.
-- Answers of other parts are inputs named for the section that answers them: `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469`, `s 673 a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed`.

§ `Section 520 -- Review of an order on the accused's application`

-- src:11573 | Review of order
-- src:11574 | 520 (1) If a judge or justice makes an order under subsection 515(2), (5), (6), (7) or (12) or vacates, varies or makes any order under paragraph 523(2)(b), the accused may, at any time before the trial of the charge, apply to a judge for a review of the order.
@ref s 520(1) (src:11573-11574)
GIVEN `the order is one made under subsection 515(2), (5), (6), (7) or (12), or a vacating, varying or making of an order under paragraph 523(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made before the trial of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(1) the accused may apply to a judge for a review of the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order is one made under subsection 515(2), (5), (6), (7) or (12), or a vacating, varying or making of an order under paragraph 523(2)(b)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a judge or justice makes an order under subsection 515(2), (5), (6), (7) or (12) or vacates, varies or makes any order under paragraph 523(2)(b), the accused may" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)
        IF NOT `the application is made before the trial of the charge` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the accused may, at any time before the trial of the charge, apply to a judge for a review of the order" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11575 | Notice to prosecutor
-- src:11576 | (2) An application under this section shall not, unless the prosecutor otherwise consents, be heard by a judge unless the accused has given to the prosecutor at least two clear days notice in writing of the application.
@ref s 520(2) (src:11575-11576)
GIVEN `the clear days of notice in writing the accused gave the prosecutor` IS A NUMBER
      `the prosecutor otherwise consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(2) the application may be heard by a judge` MEANS
    IF `the clear days of notice in writing the accused gave the prosecutor` AT LEAST 2 OR `the prosecutor otherwise consents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under this section shall not, unless the prosecutor otherwise consents, be heard by a judge unless the accused has given to the prosecutor at least two clear days notice in writing of the application"

-- src:11577 | Accused to be present
-- src:11578 | (3) If the judge so orders or the prosecutor or the accused or his counsel so requests, the accused shall be present at the hearing of an application under this section and, where the accused is in custody, the judge may order, in writing, the person having the custody of the accused to bring him before the court.
@ref s 520(3) (src:11577-11578)
GIVEN `the judge so orders, or the prosecutor or the accused or counsel for the accused so requests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(3) the accused must be present at the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the judge so orders, or the prosecutor or the accused or counsel for the accused so requests`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge so orders or the prosecutor or the accused or his counsel so requests, the accused shall be present at the hearing"

@ref s 520(3) the order to bring the accused (src:11578)
GIVEN `the accused is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(3) the judge may order in writing the person having custody of the accused to bring the accused before the court` MEANS
    IF `the accused is in custody`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the accused is in custody, the judge may order, in writing, the person having the custody of the accused to bring him before the court" (a "where" gate on a "may": ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)

-- src:11579 | Adjournment of proceedings
-- src:11580 | (4) A judge may, before or at any time during the hearing of an application under this section, on application by the prosecutor or the accused, adjourn the proceedings, but if the accused is in custody no adjournment shall be for more than three clear days except with the consent of the accused.
@ref s 520(4) (src:11579-11580)
GIVEN `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(4) the judge may adjourn the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by the prosecutor or the accused, adjourn the proceedings" (an "on" gate on a "may": the delegated ruling (c) counts "upon" as "where"; the other reading is NOTHING; name-test sweep, listed)

@ref s 520(4) the limit (src:11580)
GIVEN `the accused is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the clear days of the adjournment` IS A NUMBER
      `the accused consents to a longer adjournment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(4) the adjournment of an accused in custody is within the limit of three clear days, or the accused consents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is in custody` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the limit is stated for an accused in custody ("but if the accused is in custody no adjournment shall be for more than three clear days")
        IF `the clear days of the adjournment` AT MOST 3 OR `the accused consents to a longer adjournment` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no adjournment shall be for more than three clear days except with the consent of the accused"

-- src:11581 | Failure of accused to attend
-- src:11582 | (5) Where an accused, other than an accused who is in custody, has been ordered by a judge to be present at the hearing of an application under this section and does not attend the hearing, the judge may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused.
-- src:11583 | Execution
-- src:11584 | (6) A warrant issued under subsection (5) may be executed anywhere in Canada.
@ref s 520(5) and (6) (src:11581-11584)
GIVEN `the accused is not in custody and has been ordered by a judge to be present at the hearing and does not attend` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(5) the judge may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused` MEANS
    IF `the accused is not in custody and has been ordered by a judge to be present at the hearing and does not attend`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused, other than an accused who is in custody, has been ordered by a judge to be present at the hearing of an application under this section and does not attend the hearing, the judge may issue a warrant" (a "where" gate on a "may": ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)

@ref s 520(6) (src:11583-11584)
GIVEN `the warrant was issued under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(6) the warrant may be executed anywhere in Canada` MEANS
    IF `the warrant was issued under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant issued under subsection (5) may be executed anywhere in Canada"

-- src:11585 | Evidence and powers of judge on review
-- src:11586 | (7) On the hearing of an application under this section, the judge may consider
-- src:11587 | (a) the transcript, if any, of the proceedings heard by the justice and by any judge who previously reviewed the order made by the justice,
-- src:11588 | (b) the exhibits, if any, filed in the proceedings before the justice, and
-- src:11589 | (c) such additional evidence or exhibits as may be tendered by the accused or the prosecutor,
-- src:11590 | and shall either
-- src:11591 | (d) dismiss the application, or
-- src:11592 | (e) if the accused shows cause, allow the application, vacate or vary the order previously made by the justice and make any other order provided for in section 515 that the judge considers is warranted.
@ref s 520(7) (src:11585-11592)
DECLARE `s 520(7) what the judge may consider` IS ONE OF
    `s 520(7)(a) the transcript, if any, of the proceedings heard by the justice and by any judge who previously reviewed the order`
    `s 520(7)(b) the exhibits, if any, filed in the proceedings before the justice`
    `s 520(7)(c) such additional evidence or exhibits as may be tendered by the accused or the prosecutor`
    `s 520(7) something the list does not name`

@ref s 520(7) (src:11585-11589)
GIVEN material IS A `s 520(7) what the judge may consider`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(7) the judge may consider the material` MEANS
    CONSIDER material
    WHEN `s 520(7)(a) the transcript, if any, of the proceedings heard by the justice and by any judge who previously reviewed the order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 520(7)(b) the exhibits, if any, filed in the proceedings before the justice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 520(7)(c) such additional evidence or exhibits as may be tendered by the accused or the prosecutor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 520(7) something the list does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the judge may consider (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..." (the list does not say "only")

@ref s 520(7)(d) and (e) (src:11590-11592)
GIVEN `the hearing of the application is held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused shows cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(7) the judge must dismiss the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the hearing of the application is held` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the hearing of an application under this section, the judge ... shall either (d) dismiss the application, or (e) ..."
        IF NOT `the accused shows cause` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (d): only paragraph (d) is open when the accused does not show cause
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "shall either (d) dismiss the application, or (e) if the accused shows cause, allow the application": where cause is shown the text leaves the choice between (d) and (e) to the judge

@ref s 520(7)(e) (src:11592)
GIVEN `the hearing of the application is held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused shows cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(7)(e) the judge may allow the application, vacate or vary the order and make any other order provided for in section 515` MEANS
    IF `the hearing of the application is held` AND `the accused shows cause`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) if the accused shows cause, allow the application, vacate or vary the order previously made by the justice and make any other order provided for in section 515 that the judge considers is warranted" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE: only (d) is then open)

-- 520(8): "If an application under this section or section 521 or 525 has been heard, a further or other application under this section or section 521 shall not be made with respect to that same accused, except with
-- leave of a judge, before the expiry of 30 days from the date of the decision of the judge who heard the previous application." The 30 days are read as running to the end of the thirtieth day after the decision
-- (the day of the decision is day 0): an application on the thirtieth day is before the expiry, one on the thirty-first is not (fork F-30-days).
-- src:11593 | Limitation of further applications
-- src:11594 | (8) If an application under this section or section 521 or 525 has been heard, a further or other application under this section or section 521 shall not be made with respect to that same accused, except with leave of a judge, before the expiry of 30 days from the date of the decision of the judge who heard the previous application.
@ref s 520(8) (src:11593-11594)
GIVEN `a previous application under section 520, 521 or 525 has been heard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the decision of the judge who heard the previous application` IS A DATE
      `the date of the further application` IS A DATE
      `the judge has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(8) the further application is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a previous application under section 520, 521 or 525 has been heard` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an application under this section or section 521 or 525 has been heard, a further or other application ... shall not be made"
        IF `the judge has given leave` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except with leave of a judge"
        IF `Date to days` `the date of the further application` MINUS `Date to days` `the date of the decision of the judge who heard the previous application` AT MOST 30 THEN JUST TRUE   -- the application is made before the expiry of 30 days
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the expiry of 30 days from the date of the decision of the judge who heard the previous application" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a))

-- src:11595 | Application of sections 517, 518 and 519
-- src:11596 | (9) The provisions of sections 517, 518 and 519 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require in respect of an application under this section.
@ref s 520(9) (src:11595-11596)
GIVEN `the application is an application under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 520(9) sections 517, 518 and 519 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require` MEANS
    IF `the application is an application under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says they apply to an application under this section

§ `Section 521 -- Review of an order on the prosecutor's application`

