-- src:11605 | Failure of accused to attend
-- src:11606 | (5) Where an accused, other than an accused who is in custody, has been ordered by a judge to be present at the hearing of an application under this section and does not attend the hearing, the judge may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused.
-- src:11607 | Warrant for detention
-- src:11608 | (6) Where, pursuant to paragraph (8)(e), the judge makes an order that the accused be detained in custody until he is dealt with according to law, he shall, if the accused is not in custody, issue a warrant for the committal of the accused.
-- src:11609 | Execution
-- src:11610 | (7) A warrant issued under subsection (5) or (6) may be executed anywhere in Canada.
@ref s 521(5) to (7) (src:11605-11610)
