GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 521(5) the judge may issue a warrant for the arrest of the accused` MEANS
    IF `the accused is not in custody and has been ordered by a judge to be present at the hearing and does not attend`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused, other than an accused who is in custody, has been ordered by a judge to be present at the hearing of an application under this section and does not attend the hearing, the judge may issue a warrant" (a "where" gate on a "may": ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)

@ref s 521(6) (src:11607-11608)
GIVEN `the judge makes an order under paragraph (8)(e) that the accused be detained in custody until the accused is dealt with according to law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 521(6) the judge must issue a warrant for the committal of the accused` MEANS
    IF `the judge makes an order under paragraph (8)(e) that the accused be detained in custody until the accused is dealt with according to law` AND NOT `the accused is in custody`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, pursuant to paragraph (8)(e), the judge makes an order that the accused be detained in custody until he is dealt with according to law, he shall, if the accused is not in custody, issue a warrant for the committal of the accused"

@ref s 521(7) (src:11609-11610)
