§ `Section 522 -- Interim release by a judge only (the offences listed in section 469)`

-- src:11623 | Interim release by judge only
-- src:11624 | 522 (1) Where an accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469, no court, judge or justice, other than a judge of or a judge presiding in a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province in which the accused is so charged, may release the accused before or after the accused has been ordered to stand trial.
@ref s 522(1) (src:11623-11624)
GIVEN `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of, or a judge presiding in, a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province in which the accused is charged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 522(1) the court, judge or justice is barred from releasing the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence listed in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469, no court, judge or justice ... may release the accused"
        IF `the person is a judge of, or a judge presiding in, a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province in which the accused is charged` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no court, judge or justice, other than a judge of or a judge presiding in a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province in which the accused is so charged, may release the accused"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11625 | Idem
-- src:11626 | (2) Where an accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469, a judge of or a judge presiding in a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province in which the accused is charged shall order that the accused be detained in custody unless the accused, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified within the meaning of subsection 515(10) by clearly demonstrating that their proposed release plan addresses the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in that subsection.
@ref s 522(2) (src:11625-11626)
GIVEN `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of, or a judge presiding in, a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province in which the accused is charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused, having been given a reasonable opportunity, shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified within the meaning of subsection 515(10) by clearly demonstrating that their proposed release plan addresses the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 522(2) the judge must order that the accused be detained in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence listed in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469, a judge of or a judge presiding in a superior court of criminal jurisdiction ... shall order that the accused be detained in custody"
        IF NOT `the person is a judge of, or a judge presiding in, a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province in which the accused is charged` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a judge of or a judge presiding in a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province in which the accused is charged shall order"
        IF `the accused, having been given a reasonable opportunity, shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified within the meaning of subsection 515(10) by clearly demonstrating that their proposed release plan addresses the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in that subsection`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11627 | Order re no communication
-- src:11628 | (2.1) A judge referred to in subsection (2) who orders that an accused be detained in custody under this section may include in the order a direction that the accused abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order except in accordance with such conditions specified in the order as the judge considers necessary.
@ref s 522(2.1) (src:11627-11628)
GIVEN `the judge referred to in subsection (2) orders that the accused be detained in custody under section 522` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 522(2.1) the judge may include in the order a direction that the accused abstain from communicating with any victim, witness or other person` MEANS
    IF `the judge referred to in subsection (2) orders that the accused be detained in custody under section 522`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge referred to in subsection (2) who orders that an accused be detained in custody under this section may include in the order a direction" (a "may" for a judge who orders detention)

-- src:11629 | Release of accused
-- src:11630 | (3) If the judge does not order that the accused be detained in custody under subsection (2), the judge may make a release order referred to in section 515.
@ref s 522(3) (src:11629-11630)
GIVEN `the judge does not order that the accused be detained in custody under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 522(3) the judge may make a release order referred to in section 515` MEANS
    IF `the judge does not order that the accused be detained in custody under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the judge does not order that the accused be detained in custody under subsection (2), the judge may make a release order referred to in section 515" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)

-- src:11631 | Non-application
-- src:11632 | (3.1) For the purposes of subsection (3), subsection 515(2.01) does not apply to an accused referred to in subsection (2).
@ref s 522(3.1) (src:11631-11632)
GIVEN `the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 522(3.1) subsection 515(2.01) applies to the accused` MEANS
    IF `the accused is one referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection 515(2.01) does not apply to an accused referred to in subsection (2)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3.1) says only that subsection 515(2.01) does not apply to an accused referred to in subsection (2)

-- src:11633 | Order not reviewable except under section 680
-- src:11634 | (4) An order made under this section is not subject to review, except as provided in section 680.
@ref s 522(4) (src:11633-11634)
GIVEN `the order is made under section 522` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the review is one provided for in section 680` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 522(4) the order is subject to review other than under section 680` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under section 522`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order made under this section is not subject to review, except as provided in section 680" (review under section 680 is outside this range and the answer for it is not given here)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection is about an order made under section 522

-- src:11635 | Application of sections 517, 518 and 519
-- src:11636 | (5) The provisions of sections 517, 518 except subsection (2) thereof, and 519 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require in respect of an application for an order under subsection (2).
@ref s 522(5) (src:11635-11636)
GIVEN `the application is for an order under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 522(5) subsection 518(2) applies to the application` MEANS
    IF `the application is for an order under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of sections 517, 518 except subsection (2) thereof, and 519 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require in respect of an application for an order under subsection (2)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (5) is about an application for an order under subsection (2)

@ref s 522(5) the other provisions (src:11636)
GIVEN `the application is for an order under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 522(5) sections 517 and 519, and section 518 except subsection (2), apply with such modifications as the circumstances require` MEANS
    IF `the application is for an order under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (5) is about an application for an order under subsection (2)

-- src:11637 | Other offences
-- src:11638 | (6) Where an accused is charged with an offence mentioned in section 469 and with any other offence, a judge acting under this section may apply the provisions of this Part respecting judicial interim release to that other offence.
@ref s 522(6) (src:11637-11638)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with an offence mentioned in section 469 and with any other offence, and the judge is acting under section 522` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 522(6) the judge may apply the provisions of this Part respecting judicial interim release to the other offence` MEANS
    IF `the accused is charged with an offence mentioned in section 469 and with any other offence, and the judge is acting under section 522`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is charged with an offence mentioned in section 469 and with any other offence, a judge acting under this section may apply the provisions of this Part" (a "where" gate on a "may": ruling (b); the other reading is NOTHING)

§ `Section 523 -- How long an appearance notice, summons, undertaking or release order lasts`

-- src:11639 | Period for which appearance notice, etc., continues in force
-- src:11640 | 523 (1) Subject to subsection (2), if an accused, in respect of an offence with which they are charged, has not been taken into custody or has been released from custody under any provision of this Part, the appearance notice, summons, undertaking or release order issued to, given or entered into by the accused continues in force, subject to its terms, and applies in respect of any new information charging the same offence or an included offence that was received after the appearance notice, summons, undertaking or release order was issued, given or entered into,
-- src:11641 | (a) if the accused is, at their trial, determined to be guilty of an offence listed in section 469, until their trial is completed;
-- src:11642 | (b) if the accused is, at their trial, determined to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, until a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed on the accused; or
-- src:11643 | (c) in any other case, until their trial is completed.
@ref s 523(1) (src:11639-11643)
DECLARE `s 523(1) how the accused is determined at trial` IS ONE OF
    `s 523(1)(a) determined to be guilty of an offence listed in section 469`
    `s 523(1)(b) determined to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469`
    `s 523(1)(c) in any other case`

@ref s 523(1) (src:11639-11643)
GIVEN `the accused has not been taken into custody, or has been released from custody under a provision of this Part, in respect of an offence with which they are charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      outcome IS A `s 523(1) how the accused is determined at trial`
      `the trial is completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 673 a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed on the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order has been vacated under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(1) the appearance notice, summons, undertaking or release order continues in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused has not been taken into custody, or has been released from custody under a provision of this Part, in respect of an offence with which they are charged`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an accused, in respect of an offence with which they are charged, has not been taken into custody or has been released from custody under any provision of this Part, the appearance notice, summons, undertaking or release order ... continues in force"
        IF `the order has been vacated under subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2)" (subsection (2): the court, judge or justice "may, on cause being shown, vacate or vary any order previously made under this Part")
        IF outcome EQUALS `s 523(1)(b) determined to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469` AND `s 673 a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed on the accused`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) ... until a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed on the accused"
        IF outcome EQUALS `s 523(1)(b) determined to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the trial is completed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) ... until their trial is completed" and "(c) in any other case, until their trial is completed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11644 | When new information is received
-- src:11645 | (1.1) If an accused is charged with an offence and a new information, charging the same offence or an included offence, is received while the accused is subject to an order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking, section 507 or 508, as the case may be, does not apply in respect of the new information and the order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking applies in respect of the new information.
-- src:11646 | When direct indictment preferred
-- src:11647 | (1.2) If an accused is charged with an offence, and an indictment is preferred under section 577 charging the same offence or an included offence while the accused is subject to an order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking, the order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking applies in respect of the indictment.
@ref s 523(1.1) and (1.2) (src:11644-11647)
GIVEN `a new information charging the same offence or an included offence is received while the accused is subject to an order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(1.1) section 507 or 508 applies to the new information` MEANS
    IF `a new information charging the same offence or an included offence is received while the accused is subject to an order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "section 507 or 508, as the case may be, does not apply in respect of the new information"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1.1) says only that section 507 or 508 does not apply in that case

@ref s 523(1.1) the order applies (src:11645)
GIVEN `a new information charging the same offence or an included offence is received while the accused is subject to an order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(1.1) the order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking applies in respect of the new information` MEANS
    IF `a new information charging the same offence or an included offence is received while the accused is subject to an order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1.1) says when the order applies to the new information and says nothing of any other case

@ref s 523(1.2) (src:11646-11647)
GIVEN `an indictment is preferred under section 577 charging the same offence or an included offence while the accused is subject to an order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(1.2) the order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking applies in respect of the indictment` MEANS
    IF `an indictment is preferred under section 577 charging the same offence or an included offence while the accused is subject to an order for detention, release order, appearance notice, summons or undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1.2) says when the order applies to the indictment and says nothing of any other case

-- src:11648 | Order vacating previous order for release or detention
-- src:11649 | (2) Despite subsections (1) to (1.2),
-- src:11650 | (a) the court, judge or justice before which or whom an accused who is charged with an offence listed in section 469 is being tried, at any time until the accused’s trial is completed,
-- src:11651 | (a.1) the court, judge or justice before which or whom an accused who is charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469 is being tried, at any time until a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed on the accused,
-- src:11652 | (b) the justice, on completion of the preliminary inquiry in relation to an offence for which an accused is ordered to stand trial, other than an offence listed in section 469, or
-- src:11653 | (c) with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused or, if the accused or the prosecutor applies to vacate or vary an order that would otherwise apply under subsection (1.1), without such consent,
-- src:11654 | (i) the court, judge or justice before which or whom an accused is to be tried, at any time,
-- src:11655 | (ii) if the accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469, a judge of or a judge presiding in a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province, at any time until the accused’s trial is completed, or
-- src:11656 | (iii) if the accused is charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, the justice by whom an order was made under this Part or any other justice, at any time until a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed on the accused,
-- src:11657 | may, on cause being shown, vacate or vary any order previously made under this Part for the interim release or detention of the accused and make any other order provided for in this Part for the detention or release of the accused that the court, judge or justice considers to be warranted.
@ref s 523(2) (src:11648-11657)
DECLARE `s 523(2) who may act and when` IS ONE OF
    `s 523(2)(a) the court, judge or justice before which or whom an accused charged with an offence listed in section 469 is being tried, at any time until the accused's trial is completed`
    `s 523(2)(a.1) the court, judge or justice before which or whom an accused charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469 is being tried, at any time until a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed`
    `s 523(2)(b) the justice, on completion of the preliminary inquiry in relation to an offence for which an accused is ordered to stand trial, other than an offence listed in section 469`
    `s 523(2)(c)(i) with consent, or on an application to vacate or vary a subsection (1.1) order, the court, judge or justice before which or whom an accused is to be tried, at any time`
    `s 523(2)(c)(ii) with consent, or on such an application, if the accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469, a judge of or a judge presiding in a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province, at any time until the accused's trial is completed`
    `s 523(2)(c)(iii) with consent, or on such an application, if the accused is charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, the justice by whom an order was made under this Part or any other justice, at any time until a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed`

@ref s 523(2) (src:11648-11657)
GIVEN route IS A `s 523(2) who may act and when`
      `the person acting holds the office the route names and acts in the time the route names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent of the prosecutor and the accused is given, or the accused or the prosecutor applies to vacate or vary an order that would otherwise apply under subsection (1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cause is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(2) the court, judge or justice may vacate or vary the order previously made and make any other order for the detention or release of the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person acting holds the office the route names and acts in the time the route names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) the court, judge or justice before which or whom an accused ... is being tried, at any time until the accused’s trial is completed ... may, on cause being shown, vacate or vary any order" (a "may" whose gate fails)
        IF (route EQUALS `s 523(2)(c)(i) with consent, or on an application to vacate or vary a subsection (1.1) order, the court, judge or justice before which or whom an accused is to be tried, at any time`
            OR route EQUALS `s 523(2)(c)(ii) with consent, or on such an application, if the accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469, a judge of or a judge presiding in a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province, at any time until the accused's trial is completed`
            OR route EQUALS `s 523(2)(c)(iii) with consent, or on such an application, if the accused is charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, the justice by whom an order was made under this Part or any other justice, at any time until a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed`)
           AND NOT `the consent of the prosecutor and the accused is given, or the accused or the prosecutor applies to vacate or vary an order that would otherwise apply under subsection (1.1)`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused or, if the accused or the prosecutor applies to vacate or vary an order that would otherwise apply under subsection (1.1), without such consent" (a "may" whose gate fails)
        IF `cause is shown` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, on cause being shown, vacate or vary any order previously made under this Part" (an "on" gate on a "may": the delegated ruling (c) counts "upon" as "where"; the other reading is NOTHING; name-test sweep, listed)

-- src:11658 | Order of detention until sentencing — onus
-- src:11659 | (2.1) Despite subsection (2), if the prosecutor brings an application to vacate an order for the interim release of the accused after the accused is, at their trial, determined to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469 and before a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed on the accused, the court, judge or justice shall order that the accused be detained in custody unless the accused, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified under subsection 515(10) by clearly demonstrating that their proposed release plan addresses the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in that subsection.
@ref s 523(2.1) (src:11658-11659)
GIVEN `the prosecutor brings an application to vacate an order for the interim release of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been determined at trial to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, and no sentence within the meaning of section 673 has yet been imposed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused, having been given a reasonable opportunity, shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified under subsection 515(10) by clearly demonstrating that their proposed release plan addresses the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(2.1) the court, judge or justice must order that the accused be detained in custody` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prosecutor brings an application to vacate an order for the interim release of the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the prosecutor brings an application to vacate an order for the interim release of the accused after the accused is, at their trial, determined to be guilty ..., the court, judge or justice shall order that the accused be detained in custody"
        IF `the accused has been determined at trial to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, and no sentence within the meaning of section 673 has yet been imposed` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence other than an offence listed in section 469" (section 469, and the meaning of a sentence in section 673, are outside this range)
        IF `the accused has been determined at trial to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, and no sentence within the meaning of section 673 has yet been imposed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the accused is, at their trial, determined to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469 and before a sentence within the meaning of section 673 is imposed"
        IF `the accused, having been given a reasonable opportunity, shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified under subsection 515(10) by clearly demonstrating that their proposed release plan addresses the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in that subsection`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows cause why their detention in custody is not justified"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11660 | Application — subsection (2)
-- src:11661 | (2.2) For the purposes of subsection (2), if an accused is charged with an offence listed in section 469 but is, at their trial, determined to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, the accused is deemed to have been charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469.
@ref s 523(2.2) (src:11660-11661)
GIVEN `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused is determined at trial to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(2.2) the accused is deemed to have been charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the accused is determined at trial to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence listed in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the accused is determined at trial to be guilty of an offence other than an offence listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the deeming is for an accused charged with an offence listed in section 469 and found guilty of another; the text says nothing of any other accused

-- src:11662 | Non-application
-- src:11663 | (2.3) For the purposes of subsection (2), subsection 515(2.01) does not apply to an accused referred to in subsection (2.1).
@ref s 523(2.3) (src:11662-11663)
GIVEN `the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(2.3) subsection 515(2.01) applies to the accused` MEANS
    IF `the accused is one referred to in subsection (2.1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection 515(2.01) does not apply to an accused referred to in subsection (2.1)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2.3) says only that subsection 515(2.01) does not apply to an accused referred to in subsection (2.1)

-- src:11664 | Provisions applicable to proceedings under subsection (2)
-- src:11665 | (3) The provisions of sections 517, 518 and 519 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of any proceedings under subsection (2), except that subsection 518(2) does not apply in respect of an accused who is charged with an offence listed in section 469.
@ref s 523(3) (src:11664-11665)
GIVEN `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523(3) subsection 518(2) applies to the proceedings under subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an accused who is charged with an offence listed in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that subsection 518(2) does not apply in respect of an accused who is charged with an offence listed in section 469"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- sections 517, 518 and 519 apply "with such modifications as the circumstances require"
